# CODEOWNERS — Scanipy v3.2
#
# Path-based required-reviewer enforcement.
#
# GitHub uses this file with branch protection rules ("Require review
# from Code Owners" on the main branch settings) to block merges to
# paths listed below until the named owner approves.
#
# Syntax: <path> <owner>
#   - <path> uses gitignore-style glob matching against repo root.
#   - <owner> is one or more @user or @org/team references.
#   - Last-match-wins, so put the most specific rules at the bottom.
#
# NOTE on section headers: GitLab CODEOWNERS supports `[Name]` /
# `^[Name]` section labels. GitHub CODEOWNERS does NOT — it interprets
# any line starting with `[` as a (malformed) path pattern and rejects
# it via the parser (`gh api repos/.../codeowners/errors`). Use plain
# `#` comments for visual grouping instead.
#
# TODO: this scaffold uses a single individual handle (@locus-x64) as
# the default owner. As the org grows, replace per-section with team
# handles such as @scanipy/critical-infra, @scanipy/security,
# @scanipy/docs, @scanipy/qa. CODEOWNERS treats unknown handles as
# inactive (no enforcement), so prefer existing real handles over
# placeholders.
#
# Cross-references: RULE-9 (Security Analyst reviews INV-3/INV-4
# components) and RULE-10 (Code Review approval required before merge)
# in .claude/rules/00-global.md.

# ── Catch-all ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default reviewer for anything not matched by a more-specific rule
# below. Last-match-wins, so this is overridden by the rules that
# follow.
